# Determinism

Randomness enters as **RNG state carried on `GameState`**. Drawing returns the
value *and* the next state — `nextInt(rng, n) → [k, rng2]`. There is no hidden
generator anywhere.

**Same seed, same run, forever**, on any machine. A run is fully determined by
save seed + death count + inputs, QTE inputs included (GAME.md #determinism).
Maze layouts, dice and spawns are all replayable exactly, and layout seed is
`hash(save seed, depth, death count)` (GENERATOR.md).

`GameState` survives `structuredClone` and a JSON round-trip **deep-equal**.
That means no `Set`, no `Map`, no `Date`, no class instances, no `undefined`
members. Collections are arrays in insertion order.

Determinism is not a nicety here — it is what makes a seed shareable, a bug
reproducible, and the whole balance-simulation harness possible.
